description: Git version control and conventional commits guidelines.
alwaysApply: false
---

## Commits

- Use conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `style:`, `refactor:`
- One logical change per commit.
- Never commit `assets/` build output (gitignored — built on deploy).
- Never commit credentials, `.env` files, or local config.
- Always commit `includes/acf-json/` ACF JSON alongside block PHP changes.

## Tailwind-Specific

- When adding new Tailwind classes to PHP templates, run `npm run build` and verify the class appears in the compiled CSS before committing.
- If you add a new `@utility` or `@theme` token to `sources/css/style.css`, commit `style.css` separately from PHP template changes for cleaner history.
- Do not commit auto-generated `assets/` even if Vite regenerates it during dev — use `npm run build` intentionally before a production deploy.
